.TH VULNEWS 1 "2026-05-15" "0.1.0" "vulnews"
.SH NAME
vulnews \- Supply chain vulnerability notifier for SUSE/openSUSE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vulnews
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config ]
.I CONFIG
.RB [ \-\-one\-shot ]
.RB [ \-\-source
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vulnews
is a tool designed to provide early warning of software supply chain compromises.
It monitors a set of sources (RSS/Atom feeds, JSON feeds, and the GitHub
Advisory Database), analyzes the articles using a Large Language Model (LLM) to
detect confirmed compromises, and then checks the openSUSE Build Service (OBS)
for potentially affected packages.
.PP
The tool can run either as a daemon, polling feeds at regular intervals, or
in a "one-shot" mode. When a compromise is detected and found to impact
packages in OBS, it reports the findings to standard output, including details
about affected versions and risk assessment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fICONFIG\fR
Path to the YAML configuration file. This is a required argument.
.TP
.BR \-\-one\-shot
Poll all configured sources once and then exit. The default behavior is to run
as a daemon.
.TP
.BR \-\-source " " \fINAME\fR
Poll only the specified named source. This is useful for testing individual
feed configurations.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Fetch articles from the feeds but skip the LLM analysis and OBS impact
assessment stages.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug-level logging to standard error.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is written in YAML. Key sections include:
.TP
.B poll_interval
Integer. Time in seconds between polling cycles in daemon mode. Default is 300.
.TP
.B llm_type
String. Either "local" or "external".
.TP
.B state_dir
String. Path to a directory where persistent state (ETags, compromise database,
and models) is stored. Default is "./state".
.TP
.B sources
A list of feed sources, each with a
.BR name ,
.BR type " (must be 'rss', 'json', or 'github_advisory'), and"
.B url .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I state/feed_state.json
Stores caching information (ETags, Last-Modified) for the monitored feeds.
.TP
.I state/compromises.json
A simple database used to deduplicate reports of the same compromise.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Initialization error (e.g., missing config file, invalid configuration).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run as a daemon with a specific configuration:
.IP
vulnews \-c /etc/vulnews/config.yaml
.PP
Perform a single check of all feeds and exit:
.IP
vulnews \-c config.yaml \-\-one\-shot
.SH BUGS
No bug tracking system is currently specified.
